course: dictionary
lesson: 9145
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sniff has more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Ask what is happening and who is doing it. «Let an animal sniff your hand before you touch it» means smell with the nose, because the animal is getting to know your hand.
explain: Sniff can also be a noun, meaning the act or sound of sniffing. «She gave a loud sniff and wiped her eyes» shows a noisy breath through the nose, often when someone is crying or has a cold. The spelling is the same, but the clues in the sentence show which meaning fits.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out things such as drugs and explosives» means find by smell. Try "breathe in quickly through the nose" there, and it does not make sense. The meaning that fits is the right one.
fact: Sniff means to breathe in quickly through your nose, so that you make a small sound.
fact: To sniff something means to smell it, the way a dog sniffs a hand to learn about it.
fact: When you have a cold or are crying, you may sniff noisily. A sniff is the act or sound of this.
fact: Dogs know the world mostly by smell, so a dog sniffing your hand is often saying hello.
fact: Never sniff unknown liquids, glue or chemicals, because some fumes are dangerous. In science lessons, «waft» the smell towards you instead.
exercise: «Let an animal sniff your hand before you touch it.» What does sniff mean here? | *To smell something | To sneeze twice | To sing softly | To cry loudly
exercise: «She gave a loud sniff and wiped her eyes.» What is a sniff in this sentence? | A type of dog | A kind of sweet | *The sound of a noisy breath through the nose
exercise: Why should you never sniff an unknown liquid or glue? | Glue is always sweet | It is too cold to smell | It tastes bad | *Some fumes can be dangerous
test: «Detection dogs are trained to sniff out drugs and explosives.» Here, sniff out means? | Fall asleep | Wash off | Shout at | *Find by smell
test: Which sentence uses sniff as a noun? | We sniff the rose together. | They sniff the cold air. | *He gave a little sniff in class. | The dog will sniff your hand.
exam: Ruby says sniff always means to cry, because people sniff when they cry. What is the best reply? | Yes, it only ever means crying | Yes, but only at school | No, it means to shout | *No, sniff can also mean to smell something, or a quick breath through the nose when you have a cold
